<!--
  Stonetavern Launcher — v3 skin ("Battle.net" layout, warm stone identity).

  Scoping, stated exactly rather than generously: most selectors carry a v3-prefixed class, and the
  ambient ones additionally require the "Border.live" ancestor that only this shell sets. The
  exceptions, listed so nobody has to grep for them, are the classes named without a v3 prefix:
  kenburns, xfade, hearth, presence(.online/.away/.busy/.ingame/.offline). They are unprefixed for
  readability and are worn by no control in v1 or v2 today, but nothing enforces that. Give a v1/v2
  control one of those class names and it will pick these styles up; treat the names as reserved.

  Colours are StaticResource tokens from Styles.axaml (Stone / Parchment / Ember / Status) with two
  literals that a brush token cannot express: the patch-card fill (#EB161210, a token colour at a
  fixed alpha) and the hearth gradient stops in the markup. No new chroma, no glow: the same carved
  candlelight language as v1/v2, just arranged like Battle.net.
-->
<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:m="using:WowLauncher.Models">

    <Styles.Resources>
    </Styles.Resources>


    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         MOTION — "candlelight".

         Endless (runs as long as you look at it) — ALL of these sit under "Border.live":
           1. the stage breathes    (Border.live TransitioningContentControl.kenburns, 34s transition)
           2. the hearth breathes   (Border.live Border.hearth, 4s)
           3. PLAY breathes         (Border.live Button.action.breathe, 3.6s)
           4. the lantern flickers  (Border.live Image.v3flicker, 4s)
           5. the realm heartbeat   (Border.live Ellipse.v3pulse + .v3pulseGlow, 1.8s)

         Finite (plays once, then the frame is still):
           6. section cross-fade    (Panel/Grid.xfade, 0.18s + the two realm transitions in the markup:
                                     the key-art CrossFade and the realm-name CrossFade+vertical rise)
           7. friend row arrival    (Grid.v3enterrow, 0.22s)
           8. progress glides       (ProgressBar.v3progress, 0.4s — deliberate, see there)
           9. friends sidebar unfurl (Border.v3friendspanel, 0.25s — Width/Opacity/18px settle)

         The gate: ShellV3Window.axaml.cs drops the "live" class from the shell Border whenever the
         window is minimised or hidden, which unmatches 1-5 in one move. Items 4 and 5 exist here as
         v3-owned copies of Image.flicker / Ellipse.pulse / Ellipse.pulseGlow in Styles.axaml: those
         are ungated because v1 and v2 use them and neither has a gate, and Styles.axaml is shared
         and must not be changed for v3. Copying the animation is the price of not touching v1/v2.
         If you add another endless animation to this skin, it goes under "Border.live" or it is a
         defect: a launcher that keeps a core warm behind the game is the one thing this must not do.

         Durations are 0.12-0.24s for reactions and 1.8-34s for ambience; no bounce, no overshoot,
         no spring, no particle, no parallax. Only Opacity and RenderTransform move — both have
         registered animators; keyframe-animating RenderTransform is the crash documented in
         Styles.axaml, so the Ken Burns is a TRANSITION driven by a two-tick-per-minute timer.
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <!-- 1. The stage breathes. A 34s ping-pong between rest and a 6% push-in with a slight drift:
            roughly 0.2% of the frame per second, below the threshold where the eye reads "animation"
            and above the one where it reads "photograph". Composited transform, no layout pass. -->
    <Style Selector="TransitioningContentControl.kenburns">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="scale(1.0) translate(0px,0px)"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- The transition itself is gated, not just the timer that flips the class. Stopping the timer
         only stops the NEXT leg: a 34s transform started a second before you minimise would keep
         compositing for 34 more seconds behind a window nobody sees. Dropping the Transitions setter
         with the "live" class tears the running transition down instead. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.live TransitioningContentControl.kenburns">
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <TransformOperationsTransition Property="RenderTransform"
                                               Duration="0:0:34" Easing="SineEaseInOut"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TransitioningContentControl.kenburns.far">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="scale(1.06) translate(-9px,-5px)"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- 2. The hearth breathes, on the lantern's own cue shape (Image.flicker in Styles.axaml):
            same 4s period, same irregular beats. One flame, two places it shows. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.live Border.hearth">
        <Style.Animations>
            <Animation Duration="0:0:4.0" IterationCount="INFINITE" Easing="SineEaseInOut">
                <KeyFrame Cue="0%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="18%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.62"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="33%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.94"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="55%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.55"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="72%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.86"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="100%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
            </Animation>
        </Style.Animations>
    </Style>

    <!-- 4. The lantern flickers. Same cue shape and same 4s period as Image.flicker in Styles.axaml;
            this is a v3-owned copy purely so the gate can reach it (Styles.axaml is shared with
            v1/v2 and stays untouched). Worn by the titlebar mark and the sign-in card lantern. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.live Image.v3flicker">
        <Style.Animations>
            <Animation Duration="0:0:4.0" IterationCount="INFINITE" Easing="SineEaseInOut">
                <KeyFrame Cue="0%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="18%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.82"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="33%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.97"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="55%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.78"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="72%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.93"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="100%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
            </Animation>
        </Style.Animations>
    </Style>

    <!-- 5. The realm heartbeat: the status dot and its aura, v3-owned copies of Ellipse.pulse /
            Ellipse.pulseGlow for the same reason as above. The blur is a static setter (it costs
            nothing while the frame does not change) and only the Opacity keyframes are gated, so a
            hidden window paints no frames at all while the dot keeps its resting look on return. -->
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.v3pulseGlow">
        <Setter Property="Effect"><BlurEffect Radius="9"/></Setter>
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.50"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Border.live Ellipse.v3pulse">
        <Style.Animations>
            <Animation Duration="0:0:1.8" IterationCount="INFINITE" Easing="SineEaseInOut">
                <KeyFrame Cue="0%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="50%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.18"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="100%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
            </Animation>
        </Style.Animations>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Border.live Ellipse.v3pulseGlow">
        <Style.Animations>
            <Animation Duration="0:0:1.8" IterationCount="INFINITE" Easing="SineEaseInOut">
                <KeyFrame Cue="0%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.50"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="50%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.0"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="100%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.50"/></KeyFrame>
            </Animation>
        </Style.Animations>
    </Style>

    <!-- 6. Nothing jumps: the incoming section rises out of the stone instead of being stamped onto
            it. Opacity only — the outgoing section is already gone by then (IsVisible), so there is
            no double-exposure and no hit-test overlap. -->
    <Style Selector="Panel.xfade, Grid.xfade">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <DoubleTransition Property="Opacity" Duration="0:0:0.18" Easing="CubicEaseOut"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Panel.xfade.shown, Grid.xfade.shown">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- 3. PLAY breathes. The ember fill itself swells and ebbs (0.90-1.0 over 3.6s) — brightness,
            not a halo: the brand forbids a glow, and a solid slab that dims a touch reads as an
            ember far better than a blur would. Runs only while the button is actionable. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.live Button.action.breathe">
        <Style.Animations>
            <Animation Duration="0:0:3.6" IterationCount="INFINITE" Easing="SineEaseInOut">
                <KeyFrame Cue="0%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="50%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.90"/></KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="100%"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1.0"/></KeyFrame>
            </Animation>
        </Style.Animations>
    </Style>

    <!-- 8. Progress glides. The download reports every few hundred KB, so the raw value steps.
            0.4s linear catches up smoothly without ever running ahead of the truth. -->
    <Style Selector="ProgressBar.v3progress">
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <DoubleTransition Property="Value" Duration="0:0:0.4" Easing="LinearEasing"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!-- 7. Friend row arrival: a short lift out of the list, played once when the row is realised.
         It sits on the row's INNER grid, not on the Button: the button carries the .dim opacity for
         offline accounts, and an animation with FillMode="Forward" would pin that opacity to 1 and
         silently kill the dimming. Nesting keeps the two multiplicative. -->
    <Style Selector="Grid.v3enterrow">
        <Style.Animations>
            <Animation Duration="0:0:0.22" FillMode="Forward" Easing="CubicEaseOut">
                <KeyFrame Cue="0%">
                    <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0"/>
                    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,7,0,-7"/>
                </KeyFrame>
                <KeyFrame Cue="100%">
                    <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1"/>
                    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,0,0"/>
                </KeyFrame>
            </Animation>
        </Style.Animations>
    </Style>

    <!-- 9. Friends sidebar unfurl: a finite, user-triggered reveal (Width 0<->264 + Opacity + an 18px
            settle from the right), NOT an ambient animation - it plays once per toggle and cannot run
            behind a hidden window, so it sits outside the Border.live gate exactly like the section
            xfade (6) and the friend-row arrival (7) above. Width is animated rather than IsVisible
            toggled so the panel glides instead of snapping; the inner Panel is pinned to 264 (in the
            markup) so this only reveals a surface that was already laid out and never reflows text
            mid-open. 0.25s CubicEaseOut - candlelight easing, no bounce, no overshoot. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.v3friendspanel">
        <Setter Property="Width" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translate(18px,0)"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <DoubleTransition Property="Width" Duration="0:0:0.25" Easing="CubicEaseOut"/>
                <DoubleTransition Property="Opacity" Duration="0:0:0.25" Easing="CubicEaseOut"/>
                <TransformOperationsTransition Property="RenderTransform" Duration="0:0:0.25" Easing="CubicEaseOut"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Border.v3friendspanel.open">
        <Setter Property="Width" Value="264"/>
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translate(0px,0)"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ TopNav tab (Row0): active = ember underline, like Button.otab in v2 ═══ -->
    <!-- ═══ The wordmark, as the way home ═══
         It has to keep looking like a masthead, not like a button: no chrome, no fill, nothing that
         reads as "control". Only the pointer and a slight warming on hover say it can be pressed —
         the same restraint the tabs use. -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3brand">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3brand:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3brand:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
    </Style>

    <Style Selector="Button.v3tab">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FontDisplay}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="15"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="16,0"/>
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="48"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0,0,0,2"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="0:0:0.12"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3tab:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3tab:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3tab:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3tab.active">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Account button (Row0, right): quiet stone pill ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3account">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="12,7"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3account:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3account:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Realm rail (left, 72px): active = ember vertical edge 3px + stone recess ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail ListBoxItem">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <!-- Kein Ember-Streifen am Leistenrand mehr. Solange die Marke selbst eine glühende Kante
             bekommt, sagten beide dasselbe — zwei Betonungen für eine Aussage, und die Marke stand
             dadurch sichtbar aus der Mitte. Das Signal sitzt jetzt dort, wo der Blick ohnehin ist. -->
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,2"/>
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="62"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="0:0:0.12"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail ListBoxItem:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail ListBoxItem:selected /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail ListBoxItem:selected">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Realm-Marke ═══
         Eine gravierte Messingmarke, wie die Zimmermarken hinter einem Tavernentresen — kein runder
         Avatar (das ist der Chat-Programm-Reflex und sagt über einen Server nichts) und keine nackte
         Initiale im Leeren. Die Marke hat eine Kante, sitzt eingelassen in der Leiste und trägt das
         Sigel in der Auszeichnungsschrift. Der Realmname steht nicht darunter, sondern im Tooltip:
         das ist der ganze Grund, warum die Kachel wieder atmen kann.
         Randabstand 10px links/rechts = 52px Marke in einer 72px-Leiste. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.realmmark">
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="10,5"/>
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="52"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="3"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <!-- Eine Spur heller als die Leiste (StoneSurface #161210): die Marke liegt AUF dem Stein,
             sie ist kein Loch darin. -->
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="0:0:0.14"/>
                <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="0:0:0.14"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <!-- Angesteuert: die Marke fängt Licht, bevor sie gewählt ist. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail ListBoxItem:pointerover Border.realmmark">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- Gewählt: der Ember-Streifen am Leistenrand markiert bereits die Zeile; die Marke antwortet
         mit einer wärmeren Kante statt mit einer zweiten Farbfläche. Ein Signal, zwei Stimmen. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail ListBoxItem:selected Border.realmmark">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBorder}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Rail "+" add-realm glyph (custom, brand-safe, inert for now) -->
    <!-- Die leere Marke: dieselbe Form, dasselbe Maß, nur noch nicht vergeben. Vorher war das "+" ein
         nacktes Zeichen neben einer gerahmten Marke — zwei Dinge derselben Liste, die aussahen, als
         gehörten sie nicht zusammen. Als leerer Rahmen liest es sich als freier Platz, und genau das
         ist es: hier kommt ein eigener Realm hin. -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3railadd">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="20"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="3"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="52"/>
        <Setter Property="Width" Value="52"/>
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="10,7,10,0"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="0:0:0.14"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3railadd:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3railadd:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3railadd:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3railadd:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Friends sidebar collapse/expand handle ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3sidetoggle">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="6,10"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3sidetoggle:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3sidetoggle:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3sidetoggle:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Friend row: full-width hover, no ember (ember stays the primary action) ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3friend">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="8,7"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3friend:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3friend:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3friend:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Round avatar disc + its centered initial -->
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.v3avatar">
        <Setter Property="Width" Value="34"/>
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="34"/>
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
        <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="{StaticResource StoneBorder}"/>
        <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.v3avatarInitial">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FontDisplay}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Presence dot: colour from status token, chosen by conditional class ═══
         Base ellipse is 10x10; the row sets exactly one of the class flags below. -->
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.presence">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.presence.online">
        <!-- Owner 2026-07-23: "online but not in a world" = signed into the launcher, NOT playing.
             That idle-in-launcher state is the ember/orange one; actively playing (ingame) is green. -->
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.presence.away">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource StatusWarn}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.presence.busy">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource StatusDown}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.presence.ingame">
        <!-- Owner 2026-07-23: in-game friends read GREEN like the "online" convention
             (Discord/Battle.net). The "Playing <Realm>" activity line still distinguishes
             in-game from idle-online; the dot no longer needs the ember split. -->
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource StatusOk}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Ellipse.presence.offline">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Offline rows read dimmer (the account is still legible, the activity fades) -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3friend.dim">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.55"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Add-account field ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="TextBox.v3add">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="8,6"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBox.v3add:focus /template/ Border#PART_BorderElement">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Small ember "+" add button -->
    <!-- Der bestaetigende Knopf im Realm-Fenster.
         🔴 Neu gemasst 2026-08-05, Owner am Bildschirm: "button hier bei add realm auch nicht so
         schoen". Der Grund war eine Masszahl, nicht der Geschmack: dieser Stil ist fuer ein "+"
         gebaut worden (34px breit, Padding 0, Schrift 16) und traegt seit einem Umbau das WORT
         "Add". Ein Wort in einem Kaestchen ohne Innenabstand klebt an seinen Kanten - es sah nicht
         wie ein Knopf aus, sondern wie ein Etikett mit Hintergrundfarbe.
         Jetzt ein kompakter Hauptknopf im Mass der uebrigen Formularzeilen: derselbe Ember-Ton wie
         SPIELEN, aber eine Nummer kleiner, weil er eine Form bestaetigt und nicht ein Spiel startet.
         Danebenstehendes "Realm entfernen" bleibt ghost - genau EIN gefuellter Knopf je Zeile. -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addbtn">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FontDisplay}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="14"/>
        <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="110"/>
        <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="38"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="20,0"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="0:0:0.12"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addbtn:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addbtn:disabled">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.38"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Sign-in card (sidebar, signed out) ═══ -->
    <!-- Full-width stone field, ember focus ring — same vocabulary as the add-account field. -->
    <Style Selector="TextBox.v3login">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,9"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBox.v3login:focus /template/ Border#PART_BorderElement">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Primary ember sign-in button (the one strong action in the card) -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signin">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="14"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="40"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signin:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberBright}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signin:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signin:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Quiet sign-out link in the friends header -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signout">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="7,4"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signout:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signout:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3signout:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Add-account rejection line (unknown account / already added) -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.v3adderror">
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource StatusDown}"/>
        <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap"/>
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="2,4,0,0"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Compact patch-notes card (hero footer feed) ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3patchcard">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="#EB161210"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,11"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal"/>
        <Setter Property="Width" Value="228"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3patchcard:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3patchcard:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         ARMORY — a ledger page, not a dashboard.

         Standpoint (frontend-design / CORE §3, decided before any markup was written): the armory
         is the tavern guest book. Ruled lines instead of cards, hairline rules instead of shadows,
         numbers set in the mono face so columns align down the page, and ONE ember accent reserved
         for the single number that carries meaning (the score). The only colour that varies is the
         class accent on the character edge and name - it is the one piece of identity a player
         recognises at a glance. Nothing here glows, floats or animates: the play surface is the
         loud room, this is the quiet one.
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <!-- Character list rows: a class-coloured left edge is the whole selection language -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3chars">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3chars ListBoxItem">
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,0,1"/>
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusSm}"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3chars ListBoxItem:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3chars ListBoxItem:selected /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Section caption ("CHARACTERS", "ARMORY SCORE", "RAID LOCKOUTS") -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.v3caption">
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Ledger line: label left in parchment, value right in mono. The pair reads as one row. -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.v3ledgerlabel">
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.v3ledgervalue">
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FontMono}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="TextAlignment" Value="Right"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- The one ember number on the page -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.v3score">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FontDisplay}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="46"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource EmberBright}"/>
        <Setter Property="LineHeight" Value="50"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Addons ═══
         A row, not a card: the page is a list of decisions and reads top-to-bottom. The hairline is
         the only separator, the ember lives exclusively in the row's action button. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.v3addonrow">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneSurface}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="18,14"/>
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,0,10"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Install / Update: the one strong action per row -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addonaction">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="16,8"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addonaction:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberBright}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addonaction:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addonaction:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Remove: quiet on purpose. Deleting is never the thing the page invites you to do. -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addonremove">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,8"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addonremove:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3addonremove:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Quiet inline link (project page) -->
    <Style Selector="Button.v3linkquiet">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentFaint}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3linkquiet:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource EmberBright}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Button.v3linkquiet:pressed">
        <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="none"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Hairline rule between ledger blocks -->
    <Style Selector="Border.v3rule">
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,16"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Gesperrt waehrend eines Downloads ═══
         Rail und Era-Picker binden IsEnabled an Play.CanSwitchContext, sahen aber voll bedienbar aus:
         der Klick passierte nichts und der Spieler klickte weiter. Deaktiviert muss deaktiviert
         AUSSEHEN. Gedaempft statt ausgeblendet, damit die Auswahl lesbar bleibt und das Fenster nicht
         waehrend des Downloads halb verschwindet. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail:disabled">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.38"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3rail:disabled ListBoxItem">
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Arrow"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- Each row disables itself off its own ClientChoice.IsAvailable - the SAME flag the badge and
         the view-model click-guard read, one source, no risk of the three drifting apart. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.expansions ListBoxItem" x:DataType="m:ClientChoice">
        <Setter Property="IsEnabled" Value="{Binding IsAvailable}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.expansions:disabled">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.38"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.expansions:disabled ListBoxItem">
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Arrow"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Hero client toggle: only rendered when a realm offers more than one client
         (RealmEntry.HasMultipleClients).

         🔴 Neu gezeichnet 2026-08-05, Owner am Bildschirm: "client auswahl ist nicht so ui ux gut
         vor allem weil es nicht so ausschaut als koennte man es anclicken". Er hat recht, und der
         Grund ist benennbar: die alte Fassung war zwei Textzeilen mit einer Ember-Unterstreichung
         unter der aktiven - dieselbe Sprache wie die Reiter oben. An einem Reiter funktioniert das,
         weil eine Reiterleiste als Leiste erkennbar ist. Hier standen zwei nackte Versionsnummern
         frei im Bild, und eine unterstrichene Zahl liest sich als Beschriftung, nicht als Schalter.

         Standpunkt statt Vorlage: ein EINGELASSENER Wahlschalter aus Stein. Die Spur ist eine
         gefasste Fläche mit Haarlinie, also sichtbar ein Ding mit Rand; das gewählte Segment sitzt
         VERTIEFT (dunkler als seine Spur) statt hervorgehoben - eine Wahl, die man gedrueckt hat,
         nicht eine, die leuchtet. Ember bleibt eine Kante von 2px, kein Fuellton: die eine gefuellte
         Ember-Flaeche im Bild ist SPIELEN, und das soll so bleiben.

         Beim Hover hebt sich das ungewaehlte Segment leicht an. Das ist die eigentliche Antwort auf
         "sieht nicht klickbar aus": eine Flaeche, die auf den Zeiger reagiert, ist ein Schalter. ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3clienttoggle">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneSurface}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="3"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3clienttoggle ListBoxItem">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FontMono}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="11,6"/>
        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0,0,0,2"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusSm}"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="0:0:0.12"/>
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
    <!-- Der Zeiger hebt das ungewaehlte Segment an. Das gewaehlte bleibt unberuehrt: es ist schon
         gedrueckt, und ein gedrueckter Schalter, der beim Hover heller wird, sieht kaputt aus. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3clienttoggle ListBoxItem:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3clienttoggle ListBoxItem:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- Vertieft: dunkler als die Spur, in der es sitzt. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3clienttoggle ListBoxItem:selected /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBase}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3clienttoggle ListBoxItem:selected">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberBase}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox.v3clienttoggle ListBoxItem:selected:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBase}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Add-realm overlay (the "+" rail button): a carved card over a dim scrim, same
         xfade cross-fade the hero sections use, no second window. ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="Border.v3overlayscrim">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="#D90A0705"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBox.v3overlayfield">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,9"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBox.v3overlayfield:focus /template/ Border#PART_BorderElement">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource EmberDim}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ComboBox.v3overlayfield">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBase}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,9"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ Language picker in the action bar ═══
         Sits beside the ghost buttons and has to read as one of them, not as a form field dropped
         into a status bar: same flat stone, same secondary parchment, same 12px. The overlay field
         style above is deliberately NOT reused — it is a stretched input for a card form and looks
         like a hole in this row. Only shown when the installed client actually carries more than one
         language (see PlayViewModel.HasLanguageChoice), so it never appears as a dead control. -->
    <Style Selector="ComboBox.v3bar">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneHover}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ParchmentSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource BorderHairline}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusMd}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,6"/>
        <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ComboBox.v3bar:pointerover /template/ Border#Background">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource StoneBorder}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ COMING SOON rows (Burning Crusade / Wrath) ═══
         Each row's own IsEnabled is bound to its ClientChoice.IsAvailable (see ShellV3Window.axaml),
         so Avalonia's :disabled pseudo-class already keeps a not-yet-shippable build out of mouse AND
         keyboard selection - no separate click guard needed on the view side. This just makes that
         state look like a lock instead of a normal tile: dimmed, arrow cursor, same language as the
         whole-picker :disabled state above. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox.expansions ListBoxItem:disabled">
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.38"/>
        <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Arrow"/>
    </Style>

</Styles>
